course: dictionary
lesson: 1616
title: Chemistry: the science of substances
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chemistry is the science of substances. A substance is any material: what it is made of, how it behaves, and how it can change into a new substance. «Every kitchen is a chemistry lab: heat, acid and water change food into new substances with new tastes, smells and textures.»
explain: Chemistry explains the steps of a change. «A candle looks simple, but it is a little chemistry factory: the flame melts the wax, the liquid wax climbs the wick, turns into gas, and the gas is what actually burns.» Chemistry asks what is happening at each step and why.
explain: The word also has a second meaning, about people. «Chemistry between people» means they get on very well together. In sport and stories, good chemistry means a team or two friends work well together without having to think about it.
fact: Chemistry is the science of substances: what they are made of, how they behave and how they change into new substances.
fact: Heat, acid and water can change food into new substances with new tastes, smells and textures.
fact: A chemistry lab is a room where experiments with substances are done, and they must be done safely, with goggles and an adult.
fact: «Chemistry» can also mean the way substances act together, as in «the chemistry of the soil».
fact: Marie Curie won two Nobel Prizes, in two different sciences: physics in 1903 and chemistry in 1911.
exercise: What is chemistry? | The study of the weather | A kind of sport | *The science of substances: what they are made of and how they change | The study of plants only
exercise: «A candle is a little chemistry factory: the flame melts the wax.» What does the flame do? | Makes the candle taller | Cools the room | *Melts the wax | Puts out the wick
exercise: «The chemistry of the soil» means what? | The colour of the soil | How deep the soil is | *The way the substances in the soil act together | Who owns the soil
test: According to the text, what can heat, acid and water change food into? | Plastic | Ice | *New substances with new tastes, smells and textures | Bigger pieces of food
test: What must you use when you do experiments in a chemistry lab? | Nothing, it is always safe | *Goggles and an adult's help | A helmet and a bicycle | Wellies only
exam: «Good chemistry» between two friends means what? | They are scientists in a lab | *They get on very well together | They are the same height | They are angry with each other
